  "files": [
    {
      "sha": "5b720e6fa7f868ffcbc284a161f1a9986ff4d8be",
      "filename": ".changeset/auto-lock-dapp-activity.md",
      "status": "added",
      "additions": 18,
      "deletions": 0,
      "changes": 18,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/blob/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/.changeset%2Fauto-lock-dapp-activity.md",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/raw/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/.changeset%2Fauto-lock-dapp-activity.md",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/contents/.changeset%2Fauto-lock-dapp-activity.md?ref=d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63",
      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+---\n+'@shieldedtech/moth-extension': patch\n+---\n+\n+Using a connected dApp now counts as activity for the auto-lock, and the\n+default inactivity window is one hour.\n+\n+The inactivity clock was reset only by the side panel — opening it, clicking or\n+typing in it. A user working in a dApp with the panel closed produced no\n+activity at all, so the wallet locked out from under them mid-session as soon as\n+the window elapsed between two requests; only an operation actually in flight\n+was protected. Every successful connector request from a connected origin now\n+records activity, so a dApp session stays unlocked for as long as it keeps\n+talking to the wallet. Requests from origins the user has not connected, and\n+requests that fail, do not count.\n+\n+The default window moves from 15 minutes to 1 hour. Installs that have saved an\n+explicit choice keep it."
    },
    {
      "sha": "55589b5b9261bf70f6adca6585929857abc62faf",
      "filename": ".changeset/settings-persist-only-what-was-set.md",
      "status": "added",
      "additions": 22,
      "deletions": 0,
      "changes": 22,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/blob/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/.changeset%2Fsettings-persist-only-what-was-set.md",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/raw/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/.changeset%2Fsettings-persist-only-what-was-set.md",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/contents/.changeset%2Fsettings-persist-only-what-was-set.md?ref=d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63",
      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+---\n+'@shieldedtech/moth-extension': patch\n+---\n+\n+Saving a setting no longer freezes every other setting at its current default.\n+\n+`updateSettings` merged the caller's patch into the fully *resolved* settings and\n+wrote the result, so the first write persisted all six keys — including the ones\n+the caller never mentioned, carrying whatever the defaults happened to be. Every\n+unlock performs such a write (it saves the account's network), so any install\n+that had been unlocked once held a complete settings object, and changing a\n+default in code could never reach it. That is why raising the auto-lock default\n+to an hour had no effect on existing installs.\n+\n+Writes now merge into the stored object rather than the resolved one, so a key\n+nobody has set stays absent and keeps tracking the default. An explicitly saved\n+value — including `null` for demo mode — is still honoured and still wins.\n+\n+Existing installs keep the auto-lock value already written to their storage,\n+which for most is the old 15 minutes; it can be changed in Settings. Values are\n+deliberately not migrated: raising someone's lock timeout without asking would\n+weaken a security setting they may have chosen on purpose."
    },
    {
      "sha": "9700f4d0528ad6aeaf057a0d63b6757a6d944246",
      "filename": "packages/extension/README.md",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 1,
      "deletions": 1,
      "changes": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/blob/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2FREADME.md",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/raw/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2FREADME.md",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/contents/packages%2Fextension%2FREADME.md?ref=d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63",
      "patch": "@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ the release tag manually.\n ## Notes\n \n - **tsconfig deviation:** this package extends WXT's generated `.wxt/tsconfig.json` (path aliases, extension globals) instead of the repo's `tsconfig.base.json` — the base config's `rootDir`/`outDir`/`declaration` assumptions don't fit a Vite-bundled app. Run `yarn workspace @shieldedtech/moth-extension compile` for a typecheck.\n-- Wallet keys live encrypted (ChaCha20-Poly1305) in IndexedDB via `@shieldedtech/moth-browser`; the unlocked seed is held only in `browser.storage.session` (memory-backed, cleared when the browser exits). Locking is explicit — lock button, account removal, network switch; there is no inactivity auto-lock for now (its timer used to kill a sync in progress).\n+- Wallet keys live encrypted (ChaCha20-Poly1305) in IndexedDB via `@shieldedtech/moth-browser`; the unlocked seed is held only in `browser.storage.session` (memory-backed, cleared when the browser exits). Locking is explicit — lock button, account removal, network switch — or by the inactivity auto-lock (Settings; default 1 hour). Activity is panel input and any successful request from a connected dApp; the lock defers while a transaction is in flight.\n - **Settings → Network → Clear cache and resync** forgets everything synced for\n   the active account on its network — sync state, cached balances, pending\n   activity, and the network's pre-seed reference — and syncs again from genesis."
    },
    {
      "sha": "2226fcc42c65d5aab01a961d76c99f1aece8c7bb",
      "filename": "packages/extension/lib/background/connector-handlers.ts",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 6,
      "deletions": 1,
      "changes": 7,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/blob/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fconnector-handlers.ts",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/raw/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fconnector-handlers.ts",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/contents/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fconnector-handlers.ts?ref=d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63",
      "patch": "@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ import {\n   resolveApproval,\n } from './approvals';\n import { beginOp, endOp } from './sync-service';\n+import { recordActivity } from './auto-lock';\n import { offscreen } from './offscreen-client';\n \n // These methods can display an approval. Their panel-open attempt starts at\n@@ -230,7 +231,11 @@ export async function dispatch(\n   const preparedPanel = APPROVAL_METHODS.has(method) ? prepareApprovalPanel(senderTabId) : undefined;\n   beginOp();\n   try {\n-    return await dispatchMethod(origin, method, params, senderTabId, preparedPanel);\n+    const result = await dispatchMethod(origin, method, params, senderTabId, preparedPanel);\n+    // A connected dApp talking to the wallet is the user at work, even with the\n+    // panel closed; without this the auto-lock fires between two dApp requests.\n+    if (await isAllowed(origin)) await recordActivity(Date.now());\n+    return result;\n   } finally {\n     endOp();\n   }"
    },
    {
      "sha": "33e5f21b3373a05f4452c268c9d8ad65d3cfa91c",
      "filename": "packages/extension/lib/background/handlers.ts",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 6,
      "deletions": 2,
      "changes": 8,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/blob/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fhandlers.ts",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/raw/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fhandlers.ts",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/contents/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fhandlers.ts?ref=d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63",
      "patch": "@@ -217,8 +217,12 @@ export async function saveNetworkConfig(data: {\n     if (restartRequired) void startSync(nextSession, nextConfig).catch(() => {});\n     return statusFromSession(nextSession);\n   } catch (error) {\n-    // The account never moved, so the settings describing it must not claim otherwise.\n-    await updateSettings(previousSettings).catch(() => {});\n+    // The account never moved, so the settings describing it must not claim\n+    // otherwise. Only the two keys the forward write touched are restored.\n+    await updateSettings({\n+      network: previousSettings.network,\n+      customEndpoints: previousSettings.customEndpoints,\n+    }).catch(() => {});\n     if (restartRequired) void startSync(session, previousConfig).catch(() => {});\n     throw error;\n   }"
    },
    {
      "sha": "a6bbdc91ac83e0bdc5cb6ed06a2b03ace3079c3e",
      "filename": "packages/extension/lib/background/settings.ts",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 6,
      "deletions": 3,
      "changes": 9,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/blob/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fsettings.ts",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/raw/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fsettings.ts",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/contents/packages%2Fextension%2Flib%2Fbackground%2Fsettings.ts?ref=d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63",
      "patch": "@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ export const DEFAULT_SETTINGS: ExtensionSettings = {\n   network: 'preprod',\n   customEndpoints: null,\n   // A real timeout by default; users opt into \"Never (demo mode)\" explicitly.\n-  autoLockMinutes: 15,\n+  autoLockMinutes: 60,\n   // Send-to-name is opt-in: no resolver configured until the user sets one.\n   nameResolverUrl: null,\n   // Opt-in: warming costs a full chain walk in the background (~71 min on\n@@ -110,14 +110,17 @@ export async function getSettings(): Promise<ExtensionSettings> {\n \n export async function updateSettings(patch: Partial<ExtensionSettings>): Promise<ExtensionSettings> {\n   const current = await getSettings();\n-  const next = { ...current, ...patch };\n+  const stored = await browser.storage.local.get(SETTINGS_KEY);\n+  // Only what a caller actually set is persisted. Writing the whole resolved\n+  // object baked today's defaults into storage, so no default could move again.\n+  const next = { ...(stored[SETTINGS_KEY] as Partial<ExtensionSettings> | undefined), ...patch };\n   // Endpoint overrides belong to one named network. Callers that change only\n   // the id must never carry the previous network's URLs across implicitly.\n   if (patch.network && patch.network !== current.network && !('customEndpoints' in patch)) {\n     next.customEndpoints = null;\n   }\n   await browser.storage.local.set({ [SETTINGS_KEY]: next });\n-  return next;\n+  return getSettings();\n }\n \n /**"
    },
    {
      "sha": "38692d9a9048378819d0332183e161fe1ef9eaa2",
      "filename": "packages/extension/tests/connector-handlers.test.ts",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 19,
      "deletions": 0,
      "changes": 19,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/blob/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Ftests%2Fconnector-handlers.test.ts",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/raw/d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63/packages%2Fextension%2Ftests%2Fconnector-handlers.test.ts",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shieldedtech/moth-wallet/contents/packages%2Fextension%2Ftests%2Fconnector-handlers.test.ts?ref=d48206a1957af09bf17bf5e941c2b5bccb12db63",
      "patch": "@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ vi.mock('../lib/background/sync-service', () => ({\n }));\n \n import { dispatch } from '../lib/background/connector-handlers';\n+import { getLastActivity } from '../lib/background/auto-lock';\n import { grant, isAllowed } from '../lib/background/permissions';\n import { saveSession, type Session } from '../lib/background/session';\n import { updateSettings } from '../lib/background/settings';\n@@ -625,4 +626,22 @@ describe('connector dispatch', () => {\n     expect(beginOp).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n     expect(endOp).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n   });\n+\n+  // The auto-lock clock used to be reset only by the panel, so a session spent in a\n+  // dApp with the panel closed locked mid-play. A connected dApp's requests count.\n+  it('records auto-lock activity for a successful request from a connected origin', async () => {\n+    await connect();\n+    balancesGet.mockResolvedValue(serializeBalances(sampleBalances()));\n+    expect(await getLastActivity()).toBeNull();\n+    await dispatch(ORIGIN, 'getShieldedBalances', []);\n+    expect(await getLastActivity()).toEqual(expect.any(Number));\n+  });\n+\n+  it('records no activity for a request that is refused', async () => {\n+    await saveSession(SESSION); // unlocked but not connected\n+    await expect(dispatch(ORIGIN, 'getShieldedBalances', [])).rejects.toMatchObject({\n+      code: 'PermissionRejected',\n+    });\n+    expect(await getLastActivity()).toBeNull();\n+  });\n });"
    },
    {
